1:1 COMMENT "# range_forms.z -- the forms of an integer range in a `for` header."
1:68 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "#"
2:2 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "# There are three, and each says its own convention in its name. `each` is the"
3:79 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "# COUNT form: `N.each` walks [0, N), half-open, because a count is what it"
4:75 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "# takes. `upto` and `downto` are the ENDPOINT forms, `[this, to]` and"
5:70 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "# `[to, this]`, fully closed, because an endpoint is what they take."
6:69 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "#"
7:2 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "# All three hand back an ordinary iterator, so a header drives one and a"
8:73 EOL "\n"
9:1 COMMENT "# binding does too -- and the header LOWERS to a counted C loop, building no"
9:77 EOL "\n"
10:1 COMMENT "# object at all. Integers themselves are deliberately not iterable: there is no"
10:80 EOL "\n"
11:1 COMMENT "# bare `for x: N loop`, and no `.iterate` on a scalar."
11:55 EOL "\n"
12:1 EOL "\n"
